            "description": "January 2004: It's time. Along with the announcement of the deal, the President announcing his intention to bow out and endorse you has solidified your status as the frontrunner for the nomination. Howard Dean has dropped out, citing the newfound cooperation with the Iraqis as reason enough for him to issue an endorsement. Aside from a long-shot bid from Al Sharpton, you're seen as the inevitable nominee. To kick off your campaign, we need to really hit the ground running. How should we proceed?"
