            "description": "September 2004: An interesting new strategy is being employed by Republican surrogates. They know when polled, most Americans like you, even when they say they won't vote for you. That's an obstacle for them since they need to be able to effectively portray you as untrustworthy. One way thing they've decided to try is bringing up old allegations of voter fraud having contributed to your Senate victory in 1996. The idea is, Mary Landrieu is Vice President, having never even \"really won\" an election. It seems idiotic, and it is. But it's gaining some traction, and that's not something we can afford right now. "
